From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:50:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: mediatek: size the MT6797 CAM and MJC clock tables for
 their IDs

The CAM and MJC bindings number their clocks from 1, but
mtk_clk_simple_probe() allocates one table slot per clock. The highest ID in
each provider, CLK_CAM_LARB2 and CLK_MJC_LARB4_ASIF, indexes past the table
during registration and removal, and the provider rejects it on lookup. MFG
failed this way on its first load.

Set the provider slot count from the existing binding limits, as IMG, MM,
VDEC and VENC already do.
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-cam.c | 1 +
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-mjc.c | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-cam.c b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-cam.c
index e158379e5..f0c927620 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-cam.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ static const struct mtk_gate cam_clks[] = {
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_clk_desc cam_desc = {
+	.num_clk_ids = CLK_CAM_NR,
 	.clks = cam_clks,
 	.num_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(cam_clks),
 };
diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-mjc.c b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-mjc.c
index 830d5a34f..23bae47ca 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-mjc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6797-mjc.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ static const struct mtk_gate mjc_clks[] = {
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_clk_desc mjc_desc = {
+	.num_clk_ids = CLK_MJC_NR,
 	.clks = mjc_clks,
 	.num_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(mjc_clks),
 };
